  "2026-10-11T17:22:49.143Z","harness:codex",Implementation adds both existing package-owned calendar spellings and their optional polymorphic view/date slot to the exhaustive SDK tables. The independent gate tests exercise active optional versus required arity and inactive-package declaration retention for each spelling. No grammar ceiling was raised; runtime calendar behavior is unchanged.
  "2026-10-11T17:53:48.221Z","harness:codex","Final source verification: canonical sandboxed coverage (--maxWorkers=8 --retry=1) passed 10,163 tests in 798 files; exact statements 68097/68097, branches 52238/52238, functions 14040/14040 and lines 64757/64757. Full TypeScript check passed. The independent installed-package grammar census is 233/233, zero findings, 20/21 shapes. Pre-closure archives containing the latest SDK guide and calendar declarations pass unchanged base 19,995,781/20,000,000 bytes and real offline Sentry-injected 20,239,937/20,250,000 bytes, preserving 1655 first-party and 4731 runtime files. Blocking tracker-quality metadata findings have been repaired through pm; final complete static execution and post-closure generated-changelog archives are still pending, so these are source/pre-closure receipts rather than publication claims."
  "2026-10-11T18:12:47.565Z","harness:codex","Reviewed-delivery completion receipts: latest upstream pm-changelog 2026.10.5 generates and checks the four new entries under Unreleased, preserving prior release buckets. Final generated-changelog archives pass unchanged base 19996491/20000000 and real offline Sentry-injected 20240647/20250000 first-party byte ceilings; both retain all 1655 distribution and 4731 runtime files. Final tarball passes Node 24.21/26.9 and Bun 1.4.2 metadata/provenance/no-op/admission/CLI/history acceptance, public calendar signature checks and strict documentation TypeScript compilation. Live required Sentry/telemetry gate passes: 14-day Sentry critical/high/total 0/0/0, 7-day finish error rate 2.92%, missing failure codes 0. Validation is successful with inherited 170 historical resolution-field warnings; all four new closures contain immutable resolution/expected/actual evidence. No in-progress items remain. Hosted exact-head review/checks and merge are still pending, and public 2026.10.11 acceptance remains prior-release channel evidence."
